intro: >-
  This poem survives on a very old, filmy sheet of paper that
  <a href="/people/robert-davis/">Robert Abraham Lincoln "Lynn" Davis</a>
  enclosed in a letter to his daughter, Alice Josephine "Jo" Davis Jackson —
  Shannon's grandmother. Transcribed here exactly as it reads on the paper,
  spelling and all. A note in Robert's own hand, quoted in full below, explains
  its history: he wrote it years before sending Jo this copy, for a widow he
  was courting at the time — and the widow didn't believe he'd written it
  himself, accused him of copying it from a book, and the two fell out over
  it. The poem itself names her: "Cora Dear." Cora Martin is
  <a href="/people/robert-davis/#cora-davis">the woman Robert went on to
  marry</a>, on 8 July 1931 in Neosho, Missouri — and, per his own 1943 death
  certificate, the woman he was still married to when he died.
